description:
Implement message compose and send in app.js: textarea + send button, optimistic UI, Message/set create.

What: Compose area with textarea and send button. On send, add message to thread immediately (optimistic), then POST Message/set create. On error, revert and show error.

Algorithm:
1. Compose area HTML (injected by renderApp or present in index.html):
   - <div class=compose><textarea id=compose-body placeholder='Type a message...' rows=1></textarea><button id=send-btn>Send</button></div>
2. function setupCompose():
   - document.getElementById('send-btn').addEventListener('click', sendMessage);
   - document.getElementById('compose-body').addEventListener('keydown', e => { if (e.key === 'Enter' && !e.shiftKey) { e.preventDefault(); sendMessage(); } });
3. async function sendMessage():
   - const body = document.getElementById('compose-body').value.trim();
   - if (!body || !currentChatId) return;
   - document.getElementById('compose-body').value = '';
   - const tempId = 'temp-' + Date.now();
   - const optimistic = { id: tempId, chatId: currentChatId, senderId: 'self', body, receivedAt: new Date().toISOString(), deliveryState: 'pending' };
   - appendMessageBubble(optimistic);  // add to DOM immediately
   - try:
     - const responses = await callJmap([['Message/set', { accountId: 'a-self', create: { c0: { chatId: currentChatId, body, bodyType: 'text/plain', sentAt: new Date().toISOString() } } }, 's0']]);
     - const [, result] = responses[0];
     - if (result.notCreated && result.notCreated.c0) throw new Error(result.notCreated.c0.description);
     - const created = result.created.c0;
     - replaceTempMessage(tempId, created);  // swap optimistic bubble for real one
   - catch (err):
     - removeTempMessage(tempId);
     - document.getElementById('compose-body').value = body;  // restore text
     - showError('Send failed: ' + err.message);
4. function appendMessageBubble(msg): creates and appends a bubble to #message-thread.
5. function replaceTempMessage(tempId, realMsg): find bubble by data-temp-id, update with real id and deliveryState.

Defensive programming rules:
- body must be non-empty and trimmed before sending.
- Never send if currentChatId is null.
- On server error (notCreated), revert optimistic UI and restore compose body.
- textContent only for message body in optimistic bubble too.
- sentAt is for display only; server uses receivedAt.

Tests (oracle: Message/set create request/response shape from RFC 8620 §5.3 + kith-chat/src/message.rs):
- Sending 'Hello' with currentChatId set: optimistic bubble appears immediately with body 'Hello'
- On success: temp bubble replaced with real message with correct id
- On error (mock callJmap to throw): temp bubble removed, compose textarea restored
- Enter key sends message (Shift+Enter inserts newline)
